  "summary": "Enter x , y DT pairs (≥2, x ≠ 0), AC, then recall A, B, and r. Fitted curve: y = A + B/x.",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Inv fits y = A + B/x — a hyperbola that drops quickly then levels off toward A. Use for reciprocal relationships (e.g. Boyle-type pressure vs volume after rearranging to P vs 1/V)."
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "plain": "y = A + \\frac{B}{x}"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "mark": "reg-graph",
      "text": "Inverse regression fits y = A + B/x — a hyperbola. When x is small, the B/x term dominates; as x grows, y approaches the horizontal level A. Boyle-type P vs V relationships often fit this shape after rearranging."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "mark": "reg-graph",
      "svg": "img/reg/inv.svg",
      "caption": "Sample fit y = 2 + 10/x. The curve drops quickly at first, then levels off toward A = 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Input"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Open Inv regression (MODE 5, ▶, then 1), clear old data, enter at least two pairs as x , y DT. x must not be zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "keys",
      "keys": [
        "MODE",
        "5",
        "▶",
        "1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "Enter data",
      "items": [
        "SHIFT 9 → 1 EXE if replacing an old list",
        "For each point: x , y DT (x ≠ 0)",
        "AC when finished"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "lead": "Example — four points on y = 2 + 10/x:",
      "items": [
        "1 , 12 DT",
        "2 , 7 DT",
        "5 , 4 DT",
        "10 , 3 DT",
        "AC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "text": "Minimum 2 pairs. x = 0 is not allowed (division by zero)."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "After AC, recall A (horizontal level), B (reciprocal strength), and r. The fitted equation is y = A + B/x."
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "lead": "S-VAR recalls (after AC):",
      "items": [
        "A — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 1 EXE",
        "B — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 2 EXE",
        "r — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 3 EXE",
        "ŷ for a given x (≠ 0): type x, SHIFT 2 → 1 → ◀ → 2 EXE",
        "x̂ for a given y: type y, SHIFT 2 → 1 → ◀ → 1 EXE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
